WEBVTT

00:00:01.242 --> 00:00:04.753
The Cup in the Forest by Anne Collins.

00:00:04.813 --> 00:00:07.974
Penguin Active Reading Easy Start.

00:00:08.034 --> 00:00:15.817
Pear and his girlfriend Nina live in a big town in Norway.

00:00:15.878 --> 00:00:20.199
They are on holiday in the country.

00:00:20.259 --> 00:00:26.132
They are driving on a road near a big forest.

00:00:26.191 --> 00:00:31.145
It's beautiful here, Pear says.

00:00:31.205 --> 00:00:36.248
Let's stop the car and walk in the forest.

00:00:36.308 --> 00:00:42.032
But the forest is very dark and quiet.

00:00:42.092 --> 00:00:46.984
I don't like this place, Nina says.

00:00:47.044 --> 00:00:49.114
I'm cold.

00:00:49.174 --> 00:00:52.526
Let's go back to the car.

00:00:52.586 --> 00:00:58.078
Suddenly, Pear falls over a tree.

00:00:58.138 --> 00:01:00.340
Are you okay?

00:01:00.399 --> 00:01:02.419
Nina asks.

00:01:02.479 --> 00:01:05.900
Yes, pair answers.

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:10.133
Then he sees some old stones.

00:01:10.193 --> 00:01:15.306
These are very strange stones, he says.

00:01:15.366 --> 00:01:18.708
He moves them with his hands.

00:01:18.768 --> 00:01:21.931
They are very heavy.

00:01:21.991 --> 00:01:27.174
There's a hole under the stones, he says.

00:01:27.234 --> 00:01:31.081
He puts his hand into the hole.

00:01:31.141 --> 00:01:34.796
Be careful, Nina says.

00:01:34.856 --> 00:01:38.838
Perhaps an animal lives in there.

00:01:38.898 --> 00:01:43.039
Pear takes his hand from the hole.

00:01:43.099 --> 00:01:47.180
He has an old cup in his hand.

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:51.932
Look at this old cup, Nina, he says.

00:01:51.992 --> 00:01:54.884
It's very interesting.

00:01:54.944 --> 00:01:57.934
But why is it here?

00:01:57.994 --> 00:01:59.579
And look!

00:01:59.639 --> 00:02:03.175
There are some strange words on it.

00:02:03.234 --> 00:02:06.746
Nina looks at the cup too.

00:02:06.806 --> 00:02:10.399
It's beautiful, she says.

00:02:10.458 --> 00:02:12.510
She looks again.

00:02:12.569 --> 00:02:17.763
And very expensive, she thinks.

00:02:17.822 --> 00:02:22.614
The forest is very dark and cold.

00:02:22.674 --> 00:02:26.257
Let's go now, Nina says.

00:02:26.316 --> 00:02:29.327
I don't like this forest.

00:02:29.387 --> 00:02:32.778
They walk back to their car.

00:02:32.838 --> 00:02:36.712
Suddenly, Pear stops.

00:02:36.772 --> 00:02:38.554
What is it?

00:02:38.614 --> 00:02:40.525
Nina asks.

00:02:40.585 --> 00:02:43.828
Pear looks into the trees.

00:02:43.888 --> 00:02:47.672
There's a man there, he says.

00:02:47.732 --> 00:02:50.554
Nina looks too.

00:02:50.614 --> 00:02:54.998
I can't see a man, she says.

00:02:55.058 --> 00:02:57.866
Pear looks again.

00:02:57.926 --> 00:03:00.603
You're right, he says.

00:03:00.663 --> 00:03:03.434
It's only a tree.

00:03:03.494 --> 00:03:08.496
Pear and Nina drive to a small town.

00:03:08.556 --> 00:03:11.868
It's getting dark, Pear says.

00:03:11.927 --> 00:03:14.789
Let's stay in this town.

00:03:14.849 --> 00:03:17.900
They find a small hotel.

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:21.322
The people are very friendly.

00:03:21.382 --> 00:03:25.154
I like this hotel, Nina says.

00:03:25.213 --> 00:03:27.772
Let's stay here.

00:03:27.832 --> 00:03:32.411
near the hotel is a museum.

00:03:32.471 --> 00:03:38.342
We can take the cup to the museum in the morning, Pear says.

00:03:38.402 --> 00:03:43.744
We can ask the curator about it.

00:03:43.804 --> 00:03:49.206
Later, Pear can't sleep.

00:03:49.266 --> 00:03:55.407
He goes to the window of his room and looks into the hotel garden.

00:03:55.467 --> 00:04:02.116
A strange man is standing there He doesn't move.

00:04:02.176 --> 00:04:04.137
Who are you?

00:04:04.197 --> 00:04:05.878
Pear calls.

00:04:05.938 --> 00:04:08.641
What do you want?

00:04:08.701 --> 00:04:12.774
Then Nina comes into the room.

00:04:12.834 --> 00:04:16.036
There's a strange man in the garden.

00:04:16.096 --> 00:04:17.958
Pear says.

00:04:18.018 --> 00:04:19.880
What man?

00:04:19.940 --> 00:04:21.561
Nina asks.

00:04:21.620 --> 00:04:24.868
I can't see a man.

00:04:24.927 --> 00:04:31.415
In the morning, Pear and Nina take the cup to the museum.

00:04:31.475 --> 00:04:36.237
The museum curator is an old man.

00:04:36.296 --> 00:04:39.218
Do you know about this cup?

00:04:39.278 --> 00:04:41.398
Pear asks.

00:04:41.458 --> 00:04:47.141
The curator looks at the cup for a long time.

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:49.802
Where is it from?

00:04:49.862 --> 00:04:51.864
He asks.

00:04:51.924 --> 00:04:59.340
from a hole under some old stones in the forest, Pear says.

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:07.926
Take the cup back to the forest, now the curator says.

00:05:07.986 --> 00:05:13.086
But why, Pear asks?

00:05:13.145 --> 00:05:17.286
Do you see the old words on the cup?

00:05:17.346 --> 00:05:19.908
The curator asks.

00:05:19.968 --> 00:05:25.912
They say, this cup belongs to Harkon.

00:05:25.972 --> 00:05:28.854
Be careful.

00:05:28.914 --> 00:05:31.446
Who is Harkon?

00:05:31.506 --> 00:05:33.618
Per asks.

00:05:33.678 --> 00:05:39.732
Harkon is an old Viking name, the curator says.

00:05:39.792 --> 00:05:43.684
There are some Viking graves in the forest.

00:05:43.744 --> 00:05:48.123
This cup is from Harkon's grave.

00:05:48.183 --> 00:05:53.054
Take it back there, now.

00:05:53.114 --> 00:05:59.204
Per and Nina are drinking coffee in the hotel.

00:05:59.264 --> 00:06:04.676
Let's take the cup back to the forest, Per says.

00:06:04.736 --> 00:06:07.106
Are you crazy?

00:06:07.166 --> 00:06:08.666
Nina says.

00:06:08.726 --> 00:06:12.840
Why do you listen to the old man's stories?

00:06:12.900 --> 00:06:16.776
Percon is only a dead Viking.

00:06:16.836 --> 00:06:22.080
Yes, Per says, but I'm afraid.

00:06:22.140 --> 00:06:25.384
The cup belongs to him.

00:06:25.444 --> 00:06:31.680
Suddenly, Per sees the strange man across the room.

00:06:31.739 --> 00:06:34.492
Look, he says.

00:06:34.552 --> 00:06:36.144
Percon is here.

00:06:36.164 --> 00:06:39.413
He's in this cafe.

00:06:39.473 --> 00:06:45.794
Pear runs across the room, but Harkon isn't there.

00:06:45.854 --> 00:06:49.456
Then Pear goes back to the table.

00:06:49.516 --> 00:06:52.498
But Nina isn't there.

00:06:52.558 --> 00:06:56.741
And the bag with the cup isn't there.

00:06:56.800 --> 00:07:00.233
He runs to the door of the hotel.

00:07:00.293 --> 00:07:03.285
He sees Nina in the car.

00:07:03.345 --> 00:07:08.355
She is driving away from the hotel very fast.

00:07:08.415 --> 00:07:12.283
Stop Nina, Pear calls.

00:07:12.343 --> 00:07:14.844
Where are you going?

00:07:14.903 --> 00:07:17.774
But Nina doesn't stop.

00:07:17.834 --> 00:07:21.546
She is driving away with the cup.

00:07:21.605 --> 00:07:25.526
Nina drives away from the town.

00:07:25.586 --> 00:07:30.078
She is driving fast, very fast.

00:07:30.138 --> 00:07:32.628
But she isn't afraid.

00:07:32.688 --> 00:07:36.438
She is thinking about money.

00:07:36.498 --> 00:07:40.598
Money is important to Nina.

00:07:40.657 --> 00:07:44.959
The cup is in a bag near her.

00:07:45.019 --> 00:07:49.281
Nina looks at it and smiles.

00:07:49.341 --> 00:07:53.202
Pear is crazy, she thinks.

00:07:53.262 --> 00:07:58.605
He's afraid of old stories about dead vikings.

00:07:58.665 --> 00:08:01.886
But the cup belongs to me now.

00:08:01.946 --> 00:08:04.447
I'm taking it to Oslo.

00:08:04.507 --> 00:08:07.398
I can sell it there.

00:08:07.458 --> 00:08:13.742
Pear runs to the museum and finds the old curator.

00:08:13.802 --> 00:08:15.944
Where's the cup?

00:08:16.004 --> 00:08:18.156
The curator asks.

00:08:18.215 --> 00:08:22.720
My girlfriend has it now, Pear answers.

00:08:22.780 --> 00:08:26.362
That's bad, the curator says.

00:08:26.422 --> 00:08:29.391
The cup belongs to Harkon.

00:08:29.450 --> 00:08:34.207
But Hakon is dead, Pear says.

00:08:34.267 --> 00:08:42.238
Yes, the curator says, but there are strange stories about Viking ghosts.

00:08:42.298 --> 00:08:47.619
Take my car and go after your girlfriend.

00:08:47.679 --> 00:08:52.150
Nina drives for a long time.

00:08:52.210 --> 00:08:54.830
It is getting dark.

00:08:54.890 --> 00:08:58.174
There are no cars on the road.

00:08:58.234 --> 00:09:04.020
She can't see any towns, or houses, or people.

00:09:04.080 --> 00:09:11.304
Only forests, dark, black forests.

00:09:11.364 --> 00:09:17.248
But Nina thinks about money again, and she is happy.

00:09:17.308 --> 00:09:20.510
Now it is raining.

00:09:20.570 --> 00:09:25.404
Suddenly Nina sees a strange man.

00:09:25.464 --> 00:09:28.019
He is standing on the road.

00:09:28.079 --> 00:09:30.434
He is looking at Nina.

00:09:30.494 --> 00:09:34.136
His face is dark and angry.

00:09:34.196 --> 00:09:37.708
Nina screams and screams.

00:09:37.768 --> 00:09:40.100
She is very afraid.

00:09:40.160 --> 00:09:44.953
She can't stop the car and she can't see the road.

00:09:45.013 --> 00:09:49.006
She only sees the man's angry face.

00:09:49.066 --> 00:09:53.008
His eyes are cold and strange.

00:09:53.068 --> 00:09:57.294
They are the eyes of a dead man.

00:09:57.354 --> 00:10:02.350
The car leaves the road and hits a tree.

00:10:02.411 --> 00:10:05.794
Then it falls into a river.

00:10:05.854 --> 00:10:10.106
The water closes over the car.

00:10:10.166 --> 00:10:13.078
It is very quiet.

00:10:13.138 --> 00:10:20.944
The car, Nina and the cup are in the river.

00:10:21.004 --> 00:10:30.554
Later the police come and take the car from the river A policeman looks into the car.

00:10:30.614 --> 00:10:34.336
There's a girl in here, he says.

00:10:34.396 --> 00:10:36.638
She's dead.

00:10:36.698 --> 00:10:39.660
Pear is there too.

00:10:39.720 --> 00:10:43.671
He is very unhappy about Nina.

00:10:43.732 --> 00:10:47.964
Suddenly, he sees a man.

00:10:48.024 --> 00:10:52.450
The man is walking into the forest.

00:10:52.510 --> 00:10:57.608
The ghost of Harkon, pair thinks.

00:10:57.668 --> 00:11:00.360
He is very afraid.

00:11:00.420 --> 00:11:04.014
But Harkon is walking away now.

00:11:04.074 --> 00:11:06.325
He has his cup.
